window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"kassadin","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 6","text":"Riftwalk arrives — real mobility at last. But Purgatory grounds it, so blink out early and never fight low inside his zone."},{"when":"First item","text":"Your RQ burst starts to hurt while his edge fades; short trades onto his cooldowns now come out even or better."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Your window: stacked Riftwalks and the magic shield make you hard to pin — but only outside Purgatory, which still grounds the blink."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm even through five safe levels","Absorb his magic with Null Sphere","Reach two items and take over"],"foe":["Land Ashen Pursuit at 3","Ground you, then execute you","End the game before your spike"]},"early":"This is one of the friendlier lanes a scaling Kassadin can ask for: Null Sphere's shield eats his magic and answers his level-3 dash-in, so every stage through 5 is a genuinely even trade. But Ritual Nails outranges my Q 950 to 650 — I do not win the poke war. Farm, shield his engage, force nothing.","mid":"At 6 Riftwalk gives me mobility, but Purgatory grounds it — inside that zone the blink does not fire at all, so I never take a low-HP fight on his ground. Use R to escape or catch waves instead. Through first item the lane stays even as my RQ burst climbs against his fading edge; keep banking gold and levels.","late":"Two-plus items is my window: stacked Riftwalk lets me dictate engagements and the magic shield blunts Silver Stake, which hits harder the lower I already am. Blink onto him when Ashen Pursuit is down, unload, and blink away — outside Purgatory, where the ground still holds me.","whys":["Level 1 is even: your Q shield offsets the gap-closer he does not have yet.","Level 2 stays a skill trade — he pokes from 950, your Null Sphere absorbs the magic.","Level 3 is even because your Null Sphere shield answers his fresh dash-in.","Levels 4-5 stay even — Silver Stake ramps as you drop, so reset your HP.","Level 6 is even: Riftwalk arrives, but Purgatory grounds it.","First item stays even as your RQ burst rises against his fading edge.","Two-plus items: stacked Riftwalk edges it your way — Purgatory still grounds it."]});
