window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"kassadin","b":"zaahen","win":["Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"His walk-down starts and your magic shield does nothing against his physical damage — start conceding space immediately."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Riftwalk finally gives you an out. Mana is thin, so treat R as an escape hatch, not an engage button."},{"when":"His first item","text":"If you are behind he dives you under tower, and a full Determination bar lets him revive — keep your jungler close."},{"when":"Late 1v1s","text":"Even scaled, Dreaded Return drags you straight back — never side-lane into him while that 14s pull is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the denial with tower farm","Bank mana and hit 6 intact","Sidestep his W pull late"],"foe":["Ignore your shield with physical trades","Starve you of farm pre-6","Pull you back with W as you blink"]},"early":"The problem is stark: your Null Sphere shield blocks magic and his damage is physical, and The Darkin Glaive (10s) is an auto-attack reset that heals him and recasts into a knock-up. Concede the trades, catch what CS you safely can, and lean on tower — every level survived without dying is a win.","mid":"Level 6 restores some dignity: Riftwalk means Aureate Rush (10s) cannot run you down for free, though thin mana keeps any fight a coin-flip. Grim Deliverance arrives with it — 110s at rank 1, and it heals him off its own damage, so never trade into a fresh one. Demand jungle attention until you stabilise.","late":"Careful — this one does not flip like your usual scaling story. If he banked a lead he wins the side lane, and Dreaded Return (14s, 850 range) drags you back the moment you blink. Play with your team, go in only once that pull is spent, and win through waveclear and flanks rather than honest duels.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm before his walk-down pressure kicks in.","At level 2 his physical damage ignores your magic shield entirely, so he wins the trades.","Level 3 favours him: he denies your helpless pre-6 frame the farm and XP it needs.","Through 4-5 he dominates your squishy, low-mana frame before your ult comes online.","Level 6 is even: Riftwalk gives you mobility, but thin mana keeps every fight a coin-flip.","At first item, if you have been denied, his bruiser stats let him dive and burst you.","At two-plus items he keeps the lead and wins the side lane, and Dreaded Return drags you back if you blink."]});
